  "interview": [
    {
      "q": "What does this project actually do?",
      "a": "“livedocs.” shadcn component registry for livedocs.xyz It is a shadcn component registry."
    },
    {
      "q": "What language is it written in?",
      "a": "Mostly TypeScript (50% of tracked files), with JSON 39%, Markdown 3%, YAML 3%. ~125 source files."
    },
    {
      "q": "What framework, and why does that choice matter?",
      "a": "Built on Next.js 15.3.3 + React 19.1.0. Next.js gives file-based routing, server components and a static-export-friendly docs site in one deployable unit."
    },
    {
      "q": "How is the code organized?",
      "a": "A pnpm workspaces monorepo with 6 workspace(s): @frostui/docs, livedocs, @frostui/config, @frostui/registry, @frostui/tokens, @frostui/ui. Apps live under apps/, shared code under packages/ — classic separation of deployables vs. reusables."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I run it locally?",
      "a": "Requires Node >=20 and pnpm. Install, then `pnpm dev` — full commands are in the Scripts section below."
    },
    {
      "q": "Where does data come from? Is there a backend?",
      "a": "There is no backend, database or auth in this repo. It's a frontend/distribution project — data ships as static files or lives in client state."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do other developers consume this?",
      "a": "shadcn registry (`npx shadcn add …`) — consumers copy source into their own @/components/ui — vendor, don't depend Not published to npm — private monorepo — consumed via git / deploy, not install"
    },
    {
      "q": "How is quality enforced?",
      "a": "TypeScript with strict mode on. CI runs ci.yml on every push."
    },
    {
      "q": "Where does it deploy?",
      "a": "Hosting signals point to Vercel, live at https://livedocs.xyz."
    }
  ]
